tter, ≤48 chars) and an optional JSON object \`data\` (≤4 KiB). Every \`room_send\` is shown to the user for approval (never auto-approved; no allow rule covers it), so send deliberately — one consolidated event, not a stream. The result names how many peers were present, or says not_connected when this session is not in that room. Anything that must outlive the moment belongs in a republish (or the artifact database), not the room.
